From 196d602e3eac295825ef2d5296bd7ebe7bcbee54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:24:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/34] usb_webcam: stream video from UVC cameras

The UVC add-on was left out of the build, and it did not work: the
isochronous pump asked for 16 packets of 256 bytes, so every packet
of a high speed endpoint was cut short, and the data of the next
packet was read from the wrong place. Between two synchronous
transfers the endpoint had no request queued and the camera's data
got lost.

The pump now sizes each packet from the endpoint, including the
additional transactions per microframe, and reads every packet from
its own slot. Two pump threads keep two transfers in flight. Each
draws a ticket before it queues a transfer, and the data goes to the
deframer in ticket order. A transfer that comes too late, or a
packet that the controller marks as failed, drops the frame it
falls into.

The deframer collects a frame in a buffer of fixed size instead of
one that grows with whatever the camera sends. It is sized when the
stream starts, from the camera's dwMaxVideoFrameSize or the picture
size, whichever is larger, and capped at 64 MiB. A frame that does
not fit is dropped. Each start also drops what was left of the last
stream.

Also fixed on the way to the first picture:
- The endpoint loops used the interface index instead of the
  endpoint index.
- Only the first video streaming interface is used; format and frame
  indices only hold within it.
- The probe used the position in our frame list instead of the
  frame index from the descriptor, and committed the request
  instead of what the camera answered.
- The best alternate setting compares bytes per interval, not the
  raw wMaxPacketSize field.
- An alternate setting left active by an earlier run hides the
  class specific descriptors; parsing starts from setting 0.
- A start that fails is reported to the client, and the camera goes
  back to the idle setting.
- StopTransfer() lets the transfers in flight finish before it
  selects the idle setting, otherwise the pumps cannot be joined.
- The frame interval is the camera's default for the chosen size.
- 640x480 at 30 fps is suggested instead of a forced 320x240 at
  5 fps.

FillFrameBuffer() converts with UVCColor.h. The Bayer interpolation
it used before has no other caller and is removed. A frame shorter
than the format promises is now dropped instead of shown with a
black rest, and a missing frame sends no buffer at all.

UVCFrameBufferTest covers the frame buffer.

